DTSTART;VALUE=DATE;VALUE=DATE:20260918
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:-------------\nInstructions \n-------------\n\nThis reflective
  assignment will help you develop emotional intelligence by understanding 
 your behavior\, values\, and potential as a team member. The goal is not o
 nly to assess your current strengths and weaknesses but also to build awar
 eness of how your behavior affects others and how you can grow as a collab
 orative partner.\n\n--------------------\n\nCriteria for success\n--------
 ------------\n\n1. Reflect on Your Team Experiences\nThink back to a varie
 ty of team settings—academic group work\, leadership roles\, sports\, cl
 ubs\, volunteer projects\, or even family situations. Identify moments whe
 n you felt confident\, frustrated\, supported\, challenged\, or proud. Wha
 t roles did you tend to assume? How did others respond to you?\n\n2. Compl
 ete Your Personal SWOT Table\nUsing your reflection\, thoughtfully complet
 e the SWOT framework by answering the following questions.\n\nStrengths\n\
 nWeaknesses\n\nWhat do I naturally do well in teams?\n\nWhat areas of team
 work challenge me?\n\nWhat strengths do others recognize in me?\n\nWhat fe
 edback or habits might negatively affect my contribution?\n\nWhat roles do
  I typically take on?\n\nWhere do I tend to withdraw or resist engagement?
 \n\n \n\nOpportunities \n\nThreats \n\nWhat team-based skills or habits
  would I like to develop?\n\nWhat patterns\, fears\, or blind spots might 
 undermine my performance in groups?\n\nHow can I become a more emotionally
  intelligent teammate?\n\nAre there attitudes or assumptions that may limi
 t team progress?\n\n \n\n3. Draft Your Team Readiness Statement\n\nIn 3
 –5 sentences\, write a concise reflection that responds to the following
 :\n\nWhat kind of teammate are you?\nWhat support do you need to thrive in
  a team setting?\nWhat value(s) do you bring to collaborative work this te
 rm?\n\nThis will help both you and your future team members better underst
 and how to work with you.\n\nSubmit your Team Experiences Reflection\, a p
 rofessionally formatted and neatly organized Personal SWOT Table and a T
 eam Readiness Statement on Canvas\, ensuring clarity\, proper grammar\, a
 nd readability.
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:A Personal SWOT Reflection [__BEL___Self_Leadership_and_Team_Dynami
 cs]
