X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<h2><strong>Instructions&nbsp\;</strong></h2>\
 n<p><br>This reflective assignment will help you develop emotional intelli
 gence by understanding your behavior\, values\, and potential as a team me
 mber. The goal is not only to assess your current strengths and weaknesses
  but also to build awareness of how your behavior affects others and how y
 ou can grow as a collaborative partner.</p>\n<h2><br><strong>Criteria for 
 success</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>1. Reflect on Your Team Experiences</str
 ong><br>Think back to a variety of team settings—academic group work\, l
 eadership roles\, sports\, clubs\, volunteer projects\, or even family sit
 uations. Identify moments when you felt confident\, frustrated\, supported
 \, challenged\, or proud. What roles did you tend to assume? How did other
 s respond to you?</p>\n<p><strong>2. Complete Your Personal SWOT Table</st
 rong><br>Using your reflection\, thoughtfully complete the SWOT framework 
 by answering the following questions.<br><br></p>\n<table border="1">\n<tb
 ody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Strengths</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><stro
 ng>Weaknesses</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span>What do I n
 aturally do well in teams?</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span>What areas of
  teamwork challenge me?</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span>Wha
 t strengths do others recognize in me?</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span>W
 hat feedback or habits might negatively affect my contribution?</span></p>
 \n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span>What roles do I typically take on?</s
 pan></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span>Where do I tend to withdraw or resist enga
 gement?</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp\;</p>\n<tab
 le border="1">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Opportunities&nbsp\;</stro
 ng></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Threats&nbsp\;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>
 \n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span>What team-based skills or habits would I like to de
 velop?</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span>What patterns\, fears\, or blind 
 spots might undermine my performance in groups?</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n
 <tr>\n<td>\n<p><span>How can I become a more emotionally intelligent teamm
 ate?</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span>Are there attitudes or assumptions 
 that may limit team progress?</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>
 \n<p>&nbsp\;</p>\n<p><strong>3. Draft Your Team Readiness Statement</stron
 g></p>\n<p>In 3–5 sentences\, write a concise reflection that responds t
 o the following:</p>\n<p><em>What kind of teammate are you?</em><br><em>Wh
 at support do you need to thrive in a team setting?</em><br><em>What value
 (s) do you bring to collaborative work this term?</em></p>\n<p>This will h
 elp both you and your future team members better understand how to work wi
 th you.</p>\n<p><br><span>Submit your <strong>Team Experiences Reflection\
 , </strong>a professionally formatted and neatly organized <strong>Persona
 l SWOT Table</strong>&nbsp\;and a&nbsp\;<strong>Team Readiness Statement</
 strong>&nbsp\;on Canvas\, ensuring clarity\, proper grammar\, and readabil
 ity.</span></p>
