DESCRIPTION:At the end of each week\, you will be required to fill out [thi
 s logbook] (https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1OZXeyN9XqA1K8il3EVX9Xy
 BCQcQguFwCgcXlLONW5lE/copy)\n\nLinks to an external site.\n\nThis logbook 
 will help you and faculty keep track of the tasks and projects you are wor
 king on\, the amount of time you are spending on them and the skills you a
 re using or gaining.\n\nThe logbook will also serve as a tool to help you 
 complete your other module assessments this term.\n\nKindly find instructi
 ons for the logbook below.\n\nThe logbook contains three sheets: INSTRUCTI
 ONS\, COVER PAGE\, and (COPY for more weeks) WEEK 1. Here's how you can us
 e each section effectively:\n\nINSTRUCTIONS Sheet\n------------------\n\n*
  Read Carefully: Start by reading the instructions sheet thoroughly. It wi
 ll provide you with an overview of how to use the logbook\, any specific g
 uidelines set by your course\, and what is expected in your entries.\n\nCO
 VER PAGE Sheet\n----------------\n\n* Fill out ALL the cells of the COVER 
 PAGE in your own words. DO NOT re-use the points given\; those are mere gu
 ides/examples. The total marks of the Logbook is tied to the entries of th
 e Logbook.  If you omit or exclude one or more of the cells\, you will au
 tomatically obtain less marks.\n\n \n\n(COPY for more weeks) WEEK 1 Sheet
 \n\n* Weekly Tracking: This sheet is designed for tracking your weekly act
 ivities. You'll use this format to document each week of your internship.\
 n\n* Daily Activities: For each day\, record what tasks you worked on\, th
 e skills you utilized or developed\, and any notable achievements or chall
 enges.\n\n* Reflections: Jot down your thoughts on what you've learned\, h
 ow you've grown\, and areas for improvement.\n\n* Feedback: In Reflecting 
 With Composure (Reflection-in-action)\, reflect and/or have a discussion w
 ith your supervisor or group members about your weekly performance and doc
 ument your/their insights.\n\n* Additional Tasks: Be sure to document (inc
 luding providing proof thereof) meetings\, training sessions\, or any othe
 r special tasks assigned and completed during the week.\n\nHow to Proceed 
 for Subsequent Weeks\n-----------------------------------\n\n* Duplicate t
 he Weekly Sheet: For each subsequent week of your internship/VIS\, you sho
 uld make a copy of the "WEEK 1" sheet. Rename it appropriately (e.g.\, WEE
 K 2\, WEEK 3\, etc.) to keep your logbook organized.\n\n* Consistent Docum
 entation: Follow the same process for each week\, ensuring consistency in 
 how you document your activities\, reflections\, and feedback.\n\nFinal Ti
 ps\n----------\n\n* Regular Updates: Update the logbook at the end of each
  day or week to ensure accuracy and thoroughness. If you wait until the en
 d of your internship to record your entries\, you will most assuredly have
  an incomplete\, basic and lacklustre Logbook!\n\n* Reflection and Growth:
  Use the reflection sections as an opportunity for personal and profession
 al growth\, critically assessing your performance and setting goals for th
 e future.\n\nSubmission of Mid-Point Logbook Assignment\n-----------------
 -------------------------\n\n* Mid-Point Submission:\n\n* Mid-Point Submis
 sion: Submit your halfway logbook for review and feedback by October 9th\,
  at 11:59pm CAT)\, of your Skills Immersion 1 module. You will submit your
  Mid-Point Logbook as a Microsoft Excel (.xlsx) file: not a link to your l
 ogbook in Google Sheet form.\n\n \n\n 
